<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 2.3 pct in Oct 1-20 -NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 2.3 pct in Oct 1-20 -NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 2.89 billion zlotys, or 2.3 percent, in October 1-20 to 126.1 billion after a 1.2 pct rise in the whole of September, preliminary central bank figures showed.  </p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		     OCT 1-20    SEPT     OCT 95</p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)		2.3	  1.2	 3.0</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		   126.11     123.23     97.45</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)	22.65	22.39     20.84</p>
<p>  National currency		     103.46     100.84     76.61</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		    23.13	23.02     18.52</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector    72.35	70.57     53.48</p>
<p>NOTE: revised figures in brackets -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
